course: dictionary
lesson: 7226
title: The bright surface of the Sun
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Scientists give names to parts of things so they can talk about them clearly. The Sun is a huge ball of very hot gas, and the part we see shining is called the photosphere. Photo comes from a Greek word for light, so the photosphere is the layer that gives out light.
explain: «The Sun's visible surface, the photosphere, is about 5,500 degrees Celsius.» Visible means the part we can see, so this is the bright layer that sends out most of the Sun's light. It is not a solid surface like a rock. It is a layer of very hot gas.
explain: Dark patches called sunspots appear on the photosphere, so scientists watch it closely. Above it lie the chromosphere and the corona. «Its thin outer atmosphere, the corona, is over a million degrees» shows that the layer above can be far hotter than the surface, and scientists are still studying why.
fact: The photosphere is the bright outer surface of the Sun, or of another star, that we see.
fact: Most of the Sun's light shines out from the photosphere.
fact: The photosphere is a layer of very hot gas, about 5,500 degrees Celsius, not a solid surface.
fact: Sunspots appear on the photosphere.
fact: The chromosphere and the corona lie above the photosphere, and the corona can be seen during a total eclipse.
exercise: What does «photosphere» mean? | The cold dark space between the planets | *The bright outer layer of the Sun that we see | The dark spots that move across the Sun | The hard rocky centre at the middle of the Sun
exercise: «The Sun's visible surface, the photosphere, is about 5,500 degrees Celsius.» Is the photosphere a solid surface? | *No, it is a layer of very hot gas | Yes, it is made of ice | No, it is cold and dark | Yes, it is solid like a rock
exercise: Where do sunspots appear? | In the corona | *On the photosphere | On the Moon | Under the sea
test: Which layer lies above the photosphere? | The ocean | The core | *The corona | The crust
test: In the sentence, what does «visible» mean? | The part hidden deep inside | The part that is very cold | *The part we can see | The part that is melting
exam: Why is the photosphere important for scientists studying the Sun? | It is the name of a faraway star | *It is the bright layer that sends out most of the Sun's light | It is the cold outer shell that stops the Sun shining | It is a solid rock that spacecraft can land on
